&Q000490 = A šir-namgala (?) to Inana for Ur-Ninurta (Ur-Ninurta A)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.5.6.1
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.5.6.1&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div kirugu A

A.1. [...] RU mah-a-ni zag nu-sa₂
#lem: X; X; mah[great]; zag[side]; sa[equal]
#tr.en: ……, when she augustly appears, no one can keep pace with her, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

A.2. [...] X X ŋi₆ u₃-na kar₂-kar₂
#lem: X; X; X; ŋi[night]; ŋiʾunak[night]; kar[blow]
#tr.en: …… glowing in the night, …… with awe-inspiring splendour. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. [...]-a ni₂ me-lem₄ [gur₃]-ru
#lem: X; ni[fear]; melim[frightening splendor]; gur[lift]
#tr.en: The great gods are filled with fear at her ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. [X X]-ŋa₂-ni-še₃ diŋir gal-gal-e-ne hu-luh-ha im-du₈-du₈
#lem: X; X; diŋir[deity]; gal[big]; huluh[frightened]; du[spread]
#tr.en: Her …… utterances are as grand as those of @wDN{An}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. [...] X dug₄-ga-ni an-gin₇ mah {d}en-lil₂-gin₇ u₁₈-ru
#lem: X; X; dug[speak]; An[1]DN; mah[great]; Enlil[1]DN; urun[exalted]
#tr.en: and as weighty as those of @wDN{Enlil}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. {d}inana saŋ-kal me niŋ₂-nam-ma zag dib nin-e-ne
#lem: Inanak[1]DN; saŋkal[foremost]; me[Being]; niŋnam[anything]; zag[side]; dib[pass]; nin[lady]
#tr.en: @wDN{Inana} is supreme, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. ŋiš-hur nam-lugal-la šu du₇-du₇ ki-bi gi₄-gi₄-de₃
#lem: ŋešhur[plan]; namlugal[kingship]; šu[hand]; du[perfect]; ki[place]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: with multifarious divine powers surpassing the other divine ladies. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. [saŋ] gig₂ si sa₂-sa₂-e-de₃ us₂ gen₆-na dab₅-be₂-de₃
#lem: saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; us[path]; gin[confirm]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: She perfected the divine plans of kingship, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. ŋeštug₂-ga-ni nam-gub šag₄-ga-ni zid-de₃-eš-e nam-de₆
#lem: ŋeštug[ear]; gub[stand]; šag[heart]; zid[right]; de[carry]
#tr.en: so as to re-establish it, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. {[d]}ur-{d}nin-urta nam-sipad zi-ŋal₂-la-še₃ uŋ₃ šar₂-ra mi-ni-in-pad₃
#lem: Urninurta[1]RN; namsipad[shepherdship]; ziŋal[living things]; uŋ[people]; šar[numerous]V/i; pad[find]
#tr.en: and she made up her mind and truly yearned to provide justice for the black-headed and to give them stable governance. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. [...] nam tar-ra me zid hal-ha diŋir gal-gal-e-ne-še₃
#lem: X; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; me[Being]; zid[right]; hal[divide]; diŋir[deity]; gal[big]
#tr.en: From among the numerous people she summoned @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}} to be the shepherd of living beings. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

A.12. e₂-kur ki-tuš kug an {d}en-lil₂-la₂ ni₂ su zig₃ gur₃-ru-še₃
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; kituš[dwelling place]; kug[purify]; An[1]DN; Enlil[1]DN; ni[fear]; su[flesh]; zig[rise]; gur[lift]
#tr.en: She made the king whom she took by the hand humbly enter into the …… where destinies are determined, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. lugal-ra šu-ni im-ma-an-dab₅ sun₅-na-bi mi-ni-in-kur₉
#lem: lugal[king]; šu[hand]; dab[seize]; sun[humble]; kur[enter]
#tr.en: where the good divine powers are assigned to the great gods -- the @wTN{E-kur}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. in-nin e-ne-da nu an ki-a nam nu-tar-re-de₃
#lem: innin[lady]; ane[he]; nu[not]; an[sky]; ki[place]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: the holy dwelling of @wDN{An} and @wDN{Enlil} that is imbued with terrifying awe. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. an {d}en-lil₂-da barag-ge₄ si-a-na ad mu-un-na-ni-ib-gi₄-gi₄
#lem: An[1]DN; Enlil[1]DN; barag[sanctum]; si[fill]; ad[voice]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: There the goddess without whom no destiny is determined in heaven or earth sits on the dais with @wDN{An} and @wDN{Enlil}, taking counsel with them. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

@div trailer 

A.16. ki-ru-gu₂ 1-a-kam
#lem: kirugu[division notation in certain literary compositions]; n
#tr.en: 1st @fsux{kirugu}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

@end trailer

@end kirugu

@div kirugu B

B.17. an gal dug₄-ga-zu niŋ₂ mah-am₃ a-ba-a šu mi-ni-ib-bal-e
#lem: An[1]DN; gal[big]; dug[speak]; niŋ[thing]; mah[great]; aba[who?]; šu[hand]; bala[turn]
#tr.en: (@wDN{Inana} speaks:) @q[Inana,An and Enlil]{“Great @wDN{An}, your commands are great indeed: 
#etcsl: line-id=B.17

B.18. a-a {d}en-lil₂ nam gal tar-ra-zu sag₂ di nu-zu-a
#lem: aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN; nam[fate]; gal[big]; tar[cut]; sag[scatter]; di[speak]; zu[know]
#tr.en: who can revoke them? Father @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.18

B.19. {d}ur-{d}nin-urta šul a₂ aŋ₂-ŋa₂-<zu>-ne-ne DI-DI mu-un-zu-a-ar
#lem: Urninurta[1]RN; šul[youth]; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]; X; zu[know]
#tr.en: no one knows how to dissipate the great destinies that you determine. Both of you, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.19

B.20. nam-sipad zi-ŋal₂ uŋ₃ šar₂-ra du-ri₂-še₃ saŋ-e-eš rig₇-ga-na-ab-ze₂-en
#lem: namsipad[shepherdship]; ziŋal[living things]; uŋ[people]; šar[numerous]V/i; duri[forever]; saŋ[head]; rig[donate]
#tr.en: bestow permanently the role of shepherd of living beings, of the numerous people, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.20

B.21. e₂ iri{ki} du₃-du₃ kalam gen₆-ne₂ šag₄ kug-ta mu-u₈-de₆
#lem: e[house]; iri[city]; du[build]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; gin[confirm]; šag[heart]; kug[pure]; de[carry]
#tr.en: upon @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}, the youth who knows how to carry out your orders. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.21

B.22. kur-kur-re a₂ aŋ₂-ŋa₂-bi mu-un-zu a₂ gal he₂-aŋ₂-e
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]; zu[know]; a[arm]; gal[big]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: He has brought with him from the holy womb a knowledge of how to build homes and cities, and how to strengthen the Land. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.22

B.23. šibir-a-ni ki-bal he₂-en-gam-e us₂ gen₆ he₂-bi₂-ib-dab₅-be₂
#lem: šibir[shepherd's staff]; kibala[rebel land]; gurum[bend]; us[path]; gin[confirm]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: He knows how to direct all countries: let him give great commands. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.23

B.24. sig-ta igi-nim-še₃ kalam-ma rab₃-gin₇ šu he₂-em-ri-ri-e
#lem: sig[weak]; iginim[upper land]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; raba[clamp]; šu[hand]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: May his shepherd's crook make the rebel lands bow low; may he let them have stable governance. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.24

B.25. ka-ta e₃-a-ni [...]
#lem: kag[mouth]; e[leave]; X
#tr.en: From the south to the uplands may he clamp down upon the Land like a neck-stock. May his utterances ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.25

B.26. udu-gin₇ ka u₂-gu₇ ha-ba-kiŋ₂-kiŋ₂ GU₂ a naŋ ha-ba-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#lem: udu[sheep]; kag[mouth]; ugu[food]; kiŋ[seek]; X; a[water]; naŋ[drink]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: May he search out food for them to eat as if for sheep, and may he get them …… water to drink.”} 
#etcsl: line-id=B.26

@div trailer 

B.27. ki-ru-gu₂ 2-kam-ma-am₃
#lem: kirugu[division notation in certain literary compositions]; n
#tr.en: 2nd @fsux{kirugu}. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.27

@end trailer

@end kirugu

@div ŋišgiŋal C

C.28. {d}ur-{d}nin-urta mu su₃-ra₂-še₃ uŋ₃-ŋa₂ {d}utu-gin₇ dalla he₂-ni-in-e₃
#lem: Urninurta[1]RN; mu[year]; sud[distant]; uŋ[people]; Utu[1]DN; dalla[(to be) bright]; e[leave]
#tr.en: @q{“May @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}} shine forth like @wDN{Utu} over the people for long years!”} 
#etcsl: line-id=C.28

@div trailer 

C.29. ŋiš-gi-ŋal₂-bi-im
#lem: ŋešgiŋal[musical refrain]
#tr.en: @fsux{Ŋišgiŋal}. 
#etcsl: line-id=C.29

@end trailer

@end ŋišgiŋal

@div kirugu D

D.30. diŋir numun e₃ a-a niŋ₂-nam šar₂-ra-ke₄
#lem: diŋir[deity]; numun[seed]; e[leave]; aya[father]; niŋnam[anything]; šar[numerous]V/i
#tr.en: The god who made human seed come forth @noteref{An}, the father of all that is, 
#etcsl: line-id=D.30

D.31. lugal-ra gu₃ zid mu-na-an-de₂ nam mu-ni-ib-tar-re
#lem: lugal[king]; gu[voice]; zid[right]; de[pour]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: spoke favourably to the king, determining his destiny: @q[An,Ur-Ninurta]{“Chosen cedar, 
#etcsl: line-id=D.31

D.32. {ŋiš}erin suh me-te kisal e₂-kur-ra
#lem: eren[cedar]; suh[choose]; mete[appropriate thing]; kisal[courtyard]; Ekur[1]TN
#tr.en: ornament of the courtyard of @wTN{E-kur}! @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}, may the Land refresh itself in your shade. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.32

D.33. {d}ur-{d}nin-urta kalam-ma ŋissu-zu ni₂ he₂-eb-ši-te-en-te-en
#lem: Urninurta[1]RN; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; ŋissu[shade]; ni[self]; ten[extinguish]
#tr.en: May you be the good shepherd of all lands. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.33

D.34. kur-kur-re sipad zid-bi he₂-me-en
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; sipad[shepherd]; zid[right]; me[be]
#tr.en: May they attend as if to @wDN{Utu} when you deliver a just verdict. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.34

D.35. {d}utu-gin₇ di si sa₂ ku₅-ru-zu-uš igi-bi he₂-em-ši-ŋal₂-e
#lem: Utu[1]DN; did[lawsuit]; si[horn]; sa[equal]; kud[cut]; igi[eye]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: As you take your seat upon the royal dais with its firm foundations, 
#etcsl: line-id=D.35

D.36. barag nam-lugal-la suhuš gen₆-na-ba
#lem: barag[sanctum]; namlugal[kingship]; suhuš[foundation]; gin[confirm]
#tr.en: may you hold your head high, @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}. May the good crown be your glory. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.36

D.37. {d}ur-{d}nin-urta dur₂ ŋar-ra-zu-ne saŋ an-še₃ he₂-ni-in-il₂
#lem: Urninurta[1]RN; dur[buttocks]; ŋar[put]; saŋ[head]; an[sky]; il[raise]
#tr.en: Inspiring fear and trembling, 
#etcsl: line-id=D.37

D.38. aga zid-de₃ me-te he₂-em-mi-in-ŋal₂
#lem: aga[tiara]; zid[right]; mete[appropriate thing]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: O lion of kingship, 
#etcsl: line-id=D.38

D.39. ni₂ su zig₃ ur-mah nam-lugal-la tug₂-ba₁₃-še₃ he₂-em-mur₁₀
#lem: ni[fear]; su[flesh]; zig[rise]; urmah[lion]; namlugal[kingship]; ba[garment]; mur[dress]
#tr.en: may you wear the royal robe!”} 
#etcsl: line-id=D.39

