@div kirugu F

F.44. erim₂-ŋal₂-za ud-gin₇ gu₃ bi₂-ra
#lem: erimŋal[wicked]; ud[storm]; gu[voice]; rah[beat]
#tr.en: @q[An,Ur-Ninurta]{“You howl like a storm upon your enemies. 
#etcsl: line-id=F.44

F.45. me-lem₄-zu muru₉ dugud-da-gin₇ kur nu-še-ga-zu he₂-em-dul
#lem: melim[frightening splendor]; muru[rainstorm]; dugud[heavy]; kur[mountain(s)]; šeg[agree]; dul[cover]
#tr.en: May your splendour cover like a heavy raincloud the lands that are disobedient to you. 
#etcsl: line-id=F.45

F.46. barag#-barag gal-gal ni₂ er₉-e-ne
#lem: barag[sanctum]; gal[big]; ni[self]; ir[mighty]
#tr.en: Let the great sovereigns and powerful ones (?) tremble …… like solitary reeds. 
#etcsl: line-id=F.46

F.47. [...] X X gi dili du₃-a-gin₇ kilib₃-ba-bi saŋ he₂-em-da-sag₃-ge-ne
#lem: X; X; X; gi[reed]; dili[single]; du[build]; kilib[total]; saŋ[head]; sag[strike]
#tr.en: You arise like the south wind, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.47

F.48. [X X] X RA LI NE [...]
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; X; X
#tr.en: and when you have plotted against the rebel lands, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.48

F.49. {[tum₉]}[u₁₈]-lu-gin₇ zi-zi-da-zu-ne
#lem: ulu[south wind]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: when you have taken their people prisoners, then, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.49

F.50. kur ki-bal-zu sig₁₀-ge u₃-mu-e-ak
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; kibala[rebel land]; sig[put into]; ak[do]
#tr.en: O @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.50

F.51. uŋ₃-bi šaŋa-a um-mu-lah₅
#lem: uŋ[people]; šaŋar[afflicted]; lah[plural stem of tum ⟦bring⟧]
#tr.en: place the yoke on their necks in @wSN{Isin}, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.51

F.52. i₃-si-in{ki} iri me gal-gal-la-za
#lem: Isin[1]SN; iri[city]; me[Being]; gal[big]
#tr.en: your city of great divine powers.”} Great @wDN{An}, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.52

F.53. {d}ur-{d}nin-urta {ŋiš}šudul gu₂-ba ŋar-ni
#lem: Urninurta[1]RN; šudul[yoke]; gu[neck]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: father of the gods, 
#etcsl: line-id=F.53

F.54. an gal a-[a] diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄
#lem: An[1]DN; gal[big]; aya[father]; diŋir[deity]
#tr.en: has determined this as a destiny forever unchangeable for @wRN{Ur-@wDN{Ninurta}}, his attentive shepherd. 
#etcsl: line-id=F.54

F.55. {d}ur-{d}nin-urta sipad ŋiš tuku-ni-ir nam ul-še₃ nu-kur₂-ru mu-ni-in-tar
#lem: Urninurta[1]RN; sipad[shepherd]; ŋeš[tree]; tuku[acquire]; nam[fate]; ul[distant time]; kur[different]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=F.55

